WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:15.920
Katie was telling Olivia about ticks.

2
00:00:15.921 --> 00:00:20.468
"They are related to spiders," she said to her classmate.

3
00:00:20.469 --> 00:00:22.355
"And they are awful!

4
00:00:22.356 --> 00:00:33.821
Once they get on you, they crawl all over your skin until they find a nice spot and—this is the worst part—they bite you and suck your blood!"

5
00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:38.370
"WHAT?" cried Olivia. "That's horrible!"

6
00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:42.703
"Yeah!" said Katie with a silly smile.

7
00:00:42.704 --> 00:00:46.863
"We didn't have ticks in the city," said Olivia.

8
00:00:46.864 --> 00:00:48.996
"Well, now you're in the country.

9
00:00:48.997 --> 00:00:52.319
You'd better watch out!" said Katie.

10
00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:58.424
"So I should put ticks in my report about healthy skin?" asked Olivia.

11
00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:04.399
"Definitely," said Katie. "Ticks and how to avoid them."

12
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.763
"I'm so glad I talked to you," said Olivia.

13
00:01:07.764 --> 00:01:10.269
"What else should I include?"

14
00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.015
Katie thought a moment.

15
00:01:12.016 --> 00:01:16.634
"How much do you know about poison ivy?" she asked.

16
00:01:16.635 --> 00:01:20.060
"Not much," said Olivia.

17
00:01:20.061 --> 00:01:21.682
Katie shook her head.

18
00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:26.717
"Well, it grows wild all over the place," she said.

19
00:01:26.718 --> 00:01:32.707
"If it touches your skin and you're allergic to the plant's oil, you're in big trouble.

20
00:01:32.708 --> 00:01:35.135
First, you get it in one spot.

21
00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:37.551
Then, it usually spreads.

22
00:01:37.552 --> 00:01:42.245
You get red bumps that itch like crazy for days!"

23
00:01:42.246 --> 00:01:46.064
"What does poison ivy look like?" asked Olivia.

24
00:01:46.065 --> 00:01:48.838
"What do ticks look like?"

25
00:01:48.839 --> 00:01:52.143
"Let's find some pictures," said Katie.

26
00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:56.224
"Then you can make cool posters to show during your report."

27
00:01:56.225 --> 00:01:57.690
Katie jumped up.

28
00:01:57.691 --> 00:02:01.399
"I'll show you the health and science shelves."

29
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.788
"Thank you, Katie!" said Olivia.

30
00:02:04.789 --> 00:02:09.374
Soon the girls were sitting on the floor, surrounded by books.

31
00:02:09.375 --> 00:02:13.866
"Ooh!" said Katie. "Here's a big fat tick!

32
00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:16.547
He's making a snack out of that dog!

33
00:02:16.548 --> 00:02:17.912
That reminds me.

34
00:02:17.913 --> 00:02:20.154
I'm getting hungry."

35
00:02:20.155 --> 00:02:23.641
"Gross!" Olivia laughed.

36
00:02:23.642 --> 00:02:26.571
"Hey, I have a peanut butter sandwich.

37
00:02:26.572 --> 00:02:28.561
We could share it."

38
00:02:28.562 --> 00:02:32.225
"Thanks," Katie answered, smiling at Olivia.

39
00:02:32.226 --> 00:02:35.951
"She's really nice," thought Katie.

40
00:02:35.952 --> 00:02:40.195
Suddenly Mr. Dexter appeared, standing over them.

41
00:02:40.196 --> 00:02:44.329
"Katie, your sister just called to check on you.

42
00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:48.734
She said they were expecting you at home over an hour ago."

43
00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:51.689
Katie's eyes got as big as saucers.

44
00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.196
"Oh no! What time is it?"

45
00:02:54.197 --> 00:02:56.301
Katie looked up at the clock.

46
00:02:56.302 --> 00:03:01.974
"Yikes!" she cried. "I have to go—right now!"

47
00:03:01.975 --> 00:03:06.355
Katie grabbed her backpack and ran out of the library.

48
00:03:06.356 --> 00:03:11.109
She hopped onto her bike and sped home as fast as she could.

49
00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:15.171
She dropped her bike in the yard and dashed inside.

50
00:03:15.172 --> 00:03:17.749
"Here I am!" she called.

51
00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:22.624
Joy and Grandpa were sitting at the kitchen table.

52
00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:27.332
"Where are Luke and Carlos?" cried Katie breathlessly.

53
00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:30.062
"They left," said Joy.

54
00:03:30.063 --> 00:03:35.490
"What! But I have the square-dance music and—" Katie frowned.

55
00:03:35.491 --> 00:03:41.285
"Joy, what is that thing in your hand, and why are you pointing it at me?"

56
00:03:41.286 --> 00:03:46.615
"This is the friendship meter," answered Joy. "I invented it.

57
00:03:46.616 --> 00:03:51.042
Right now it is frowning because you let your friends down."

58
00:03:51.043 --> 00:03:55.370
"But I didn't do it intentionally," said Katie.

59
00:03:55.371 --> 00:03:57.430
"I know," said Joy.

60
00:03:57.431 --> 00:04:02.062
"But a good friend would call and explain what happened."

61
00:04:02.063 --> 00:04:05.482
Katie groaned.

62
00:04:05.483 --> 00:04:08.203
"Joy is right," Grandpa said.

63
00:04:08.204 --> 00:04:11.530
"You should call Luke and Carlos now."

64
00:04:11.531 --> 00:04:15.045
Katie went to the kitchen phone and dialed Luke's number.

65
00:04:15.046 --> 00:04:18.303
"It's ringing," she said.

66
00:04:18.304 --> 00:04:20.875
"Hello, Luke? It's Katie.

67
00:04:20.876 --> 00:04:29.034
I—I can explain—I know—I was working at the library with Olivia and—What?

68
00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:34.690
I never said I didn't like her! Anyway—Luke? Hello?"

69
00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:36.447
Katie stomped her foot.

70
00:04:36.448 --> 00:04:38.399
"He hung up on me!

71
00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.847
That makes me so mad!"

72
00:04:40.848 --> 00:04:43.676
She dialed Luke's number again.

73
00:04:43.677 --> 00:04:47.035
"Hello? Now I'm hanging up on you!"

74
00:04:47.036 --> 00:04:51.540
Katie yelled and slammed the phone down. "HA!"

75
00:04:51.541 --> 00:04:58.019
Joy sighed. "I've learned that friends are very important for your health.

76
00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:02.795
You could use some tips about how to make up with them," she said.

77
00:05:02.796 --> 00:05:06.433
"No, thanks!" said Katie.

78
00:05:06.434 --> 00:05:11.950
"And stop pointing that friendship meter at me!"
